    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="0599" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.512/157</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé at Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Childs</hi>)<anchor n="59" xml:id="d612-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 106</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-02">December 2, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your despatch
                    no. 364 of September 30, 1941, informing the Department that the French Resident
                    General has made formal application for the Department’s assent to <pb
                        facs="0600" n="592" xml:id="pg592"/> the application to American <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ressortissants</hi> in the French Zone of Morocco of
                    various taxation dahirs and decrees, these relating to an income tax, the
                    “patente” tax, and a supplement to the “patente” tax.</p>
                <p>You may inform the French Resident General that, subject to the reservations
                    suggested by the Legation, which should be embodied in your note to that
                    official, this Government consents to the application of these dahirs and
                    decrees to American nationals and American protected persons as of the date this
                    Government’s consent is conveyed to the French Resident General, provided that
                    they are applied also, of course, to all other nationals without
                    discrimination.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed>A. A. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Berle, Jr</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d612-f1" n="59" type="source" xml:id="d612-f1-content">
                <p>A note in accordance with this instruction was addressed to the French Resident
                    General, January 22, 1942; not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
